course: dictionary
lesson: 2760
title: Disclose: tell or show
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: To disclose something means to tell people something that was secret or private, or to show something that was hidden. It is a formal word, so you will often meet it in news, rules and safety messages. Context helps you choose the right meaning.
explain: «Children can disclose a secret to a trusted adult if someone is hurting them.» Here disclose means to tell. The trusted adult is the person you tell, and the secret is the thing you share with them.
explain: «Disclosing tablets colour plaque pink so you can see where you missed.» The tablet does not tell anyone a secret. It shows the plaque you missed when brushing, which was hidden until the colour showed it. Ask yourself: is someone telling, or is something being shown? Swap in your meaning and check it still makes sense.
fact: To disclose means to tell a secret or private thing, or to show something hidden.
fact: Companies must disclose information, and people must not disclose their passwords.
fact: «Disclosing tablets colour plaque pink so you can see where you missed.»
fact: Plaque is a sticky film of bacteria on teeth. Plaque left for days can harden into tartar, which only a dentist or hygienist can scrape off.
fact: The forms are disclose, discloses, disclosed and disclosing.
exercise: «Children can disclose a secret to a trusted adult if someone is hurting them.» What does disclose mean here? | To sing loudly | To hide something under a blanket | To forget something | *To tell someone something secret
exercise: «Disclosing tablets colour plaque pink so you can see where you missed.» What does a disclosing tablet do? | It cleans the teeth away for you | It tells the dentist a joke | It makes your teeth hurt | *It shows the plaque that was hidden
exercise: Pupil asks, «Can I disclose my password to a friend?» What is the answer? | Yes, friends are trusted | Yes, if the friend asks nicely | Only on a Monday | *No, people must not disclose passwords
test: «Companies must disclose information to the public.» What does disclose mean here? | To run away quickly | To hide a box under the bed | To paint a picture on a wall | *To tell people information that was private
test: Which word fits the gap? A dentist's pink ___ shows the plaque you missed. | sleeping pill | toothbrush | *disclosing tablet | sugary sweet
exam: Which sentence uses disclose correctly? | *The doctor must not disclose her patient's private news | The sun will disclose a happy song in the park | Please disclose the sandwich at lunch time | We disclosed a red bicycle to the moon
